#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ef881ff-71d4-5268-9cac-32c478dc02a5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regions in the Plane Where a Function Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b727039b-016b-5dcd-a554-589bc1eb5dff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/f0547f4bf2530cbcc271e81ba501c3710b0359bb222d1e56014acac6675b515d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330297} {:answer/id #uuid "3bb86582-4a82-5cc1-a06f-708fd5a7166c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/cd0a8472d9b1abff7090be8547c654f8842b6fc934f768d8c34fe208e4058990.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330298} {:answer/id #uuid "9cad1796-5cb7-5981-b480-161d04187ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/2f661772948f506a7fa8f0a205cf2e84b3a10dfc9bc35b695d572755ca35c917.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330299} {:answer/id #uuid "39bafa95-736b-5e31-ba87-57e44397aae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/1cadc33591f95b5b66f50794e329768364708bb7f9de1e06d579ff1833be11d4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330300} {:answer/id #uuid "be469f9c-054d-55d1-b764-7ba7fd34b7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/7c1521cfad08f4c1cc4a699066ec5dc84fd635c2f1d39f71dca5a8ba86533887.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bb86582-4a82-5cc1-a06f-708fd5a7166c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/cd0a8472d9b1abff7090be8547c654f8842b6fc934f768d8c34fe208e4058990.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330298} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6ad0811-692c-57bd-90a9-0db23570a47d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3557c58-b79b-5ef1-8132-f7d04ee3b456" :question/math-academy-id "q-149550" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)=(3-x){y}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)<0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=3$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have a strict inequality, we use dashed lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/e4d289aef282e076b062aab6d8f0f209396313e2c6403b2e27d1c0272ac90795.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/4cef3532a8e70098c030f2341800f06e9e54e4074126a0a97aecdf1f1c5185d0.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(3-x)$ | ${y}^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(2,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(4,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(2,-1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(4,-1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)<0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/c9ed172c5746b1b0afd2d9b7b3bbb21245115df164bfb7e34f4f530887376e28.png)"}]}
